      "refersTo": "menu",
      "description": "Teleported right-click menu; rows highlight in system blue.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-menu\"><div class=\"ds-menu-label\">a1b2c3d — Fix graph lanes</div><button class=\"ds-item\">Copy short SHA</button><button class=\"ds-item\">Create branch here…</button><div class=\"ds-div\"></div><button class=\"ds-item ds-danger-item\">Hard — discard all changes</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-menu{width:230px;padding:4px 0;background:var(--surface-overlay,#2e2e31);border:1px solid var(--border,#3c3c40);border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.5);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-menu-label{padding:5px 12px;font:11px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',Menlo,monospace;color:var(--text-tertiary,#a1a1a6)}.ds-item{display:block;width:100%;padding:6px 12px;border:none;background:none;text-align:left;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-primary,#e8e8ea);cursor:pointer}.ds-item:hover,.ds-item:focus-visible{background:var(--accent-fill,#2f6fdc);color:#fff;outline:none}.ds-danger-item{color:var(--danger,#ff7b72)}.ds-div{height:1px;margin:3px 0;background:var(--border-subtle,#303033)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ref Labels",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "label-branch",
      "description": "HEAD, branch, remote, tag and stash labels in the commit graph.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-l ds-head\">HEAD</span> <span class=\"ds-l ds-branch\">main</span> <span class=\"ds-l ds-remote\">origin/main</span> <span class=\"ds-l ds-tag\">v1.2.0</span> <span class=\"ds-l ds-stash\">stash@{0}</span>",
      "css": ".ds-l{display:inline-block;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px;font:500 11px -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;border:1px solid transparent}.ds-head{background:var(--accent-fill,#2f6fdc);color:#fff}.ds-branch{background:rgba(90,165,255,.13);color:var(--accent-text,#5aa5ff);border-color:rgba(90,165,255,.4)}.ds-remote{background:var(--surface-control,#38383c);color:var(--text-secondary,#c0c0c5);border-color:var(--border-strong,#4c4c51)}.ds-tag{background:rgba(227,179,65,.14);color:var(--tag,#e3b341);border-color:rgba(227,179,65,.35)}.ds-stash{background:rgba(190,150,239,.14);color:var(--stash,#be96ef);border-color:rgba(190,150,239,.35)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Diff Lines",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Signature component: SF Mono diff on the Ink Well surface.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-diff\"><div class=\"ds-h\">@@ -12,3 +12,4 @@</div><div class=\"ds-ln\"><span>12</span><span>12</span><code> func layout() {</code></div><div class=\"ds-ln ds-del\"><span>13</span><span></span><code>-  colors := legacy</code></div><div class=\"ds-ln ds-add\"><span></span><span>13</span><code>+  colors := laneColors</code></div><div class=\"ds-ln ds-add\"><span></span><span>14</span><code>+  return build(colors)</code></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-diff{width:340px;background:var(--surface-sunken,#141416);font:12px/19px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',Menlo,monospace;color:var(--text-secondary,#c0c0c5)}.ds-h{padding:3px 10px;background:var(--surface-raised,#222225);color:var(--text-tertiary,#a1a1a6);font-size:11px}.ds-ln{display:flex;white-space:pre}.ds-ln span{width:36px;padding-right:6px;text-align:right;font-size:11px;color:var(--text-tertiary,#a1a1a6)}.ds-ln code{font:inherit;padding-left:6px}.ds-add{background:rgba(79,201,119,.09)}.ds-add code{color:var(--add-fg,#b6ecc6)}.ds-del{background:rgba(255,123,114,.09)}.ds-del code{color:var(--del-fg,#ffbdb7)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Lab Notebook",
    "overview": "Burlwood is where a developer reads what happened and decides what happens next. The notebook metaphor sets the priorities: the entries (commit history, diffs, conflicts) are the content, and everything around them is the binding. It should be quiet, neutral, and steady enough to read for hours. The chrome uses macOS's own vocabulary (system fonts, neutral greys, system-blue actions, blue-highlighted menus) so the app feels at home next to Xcode and Finder rather than like a themed web page.\n\nColour is reserved for meaning. A green line was added and a red line was removed. Orange is a modified file. Blue is the thing you can act on. If a colour does not carry one of those meanings, it should not be there. The UI is dense because git work is dense, but it is never cramped: text stays at or above 11px, every text level clears 4.5:1 contrast, and code gets its own monospace voice.\n\nDestructive operations are written like careful notebook corrections: they name their consequence and can be undone where git allows (discard and hard reset show an Undo toast). Anything that can't be undone, such as force-pushing or force-deleting, gets its own explicit, red-filled step.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Neutral grey surfaces layered by tone, not by borders or shadows",
      "One accent (system blue) for actions, focus and selection",
      "Git semantics own the remaining colour: add, delete, modified, untracked, ours/theirs, tag, stash",
      "SF Pro for the interface, SF Mono for anything copied from or into git",
      "Four text sizes, no decorative type"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaning-Only Rule",
        "body": "Every hue in the interface must map to a git state or an action. A new colour needs a new meaning.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Shared-Red Rule",
        "body": "Red means removal or destruction, never a neutral action. Unstage is blue, not red. Graph lanes never use the add or delete hues.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token Rule",
        "body": "Components use `var(--token)` from `frontend/src/style.css`. A hex value in a component is a bug.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Sizes Rule",
        "body": "Text uses `--text-meta`, `--text-row`, `--text-body` or `--text-title`. The only exceptions are the 32px welcome wordmark and 16px glyph icons.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Real Mono Rule",
